.TH SDL_PutAudioStreamPlanarData 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_PutAudioStreamPlanarData \- Add data to the stream with each channel in a separate array.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_audio.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_PutAudioStreamPlanarData(SDL_AudioStream *stream, const void * const *channel_buffers, int num_channels, int num_samples);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This data must match the format/channels/samplerate specified in the latest call to
.BR SDL_SetAudioStreamFormat ,
or the format specified when creating the stream if it hasn\(aqt been changed\[char46]
.PP
The data will be interleaved and queued\[char46] Note that
.BR SDL_AudioStream
only operates on interleaved data, so this is simply a convenience function for easily queueing data from sources that provide separate arrays\[char46] There is no equivalent function to retrieve planar data\[char46]
.PP
The arrays in
.BR channel_buffers
are ordered as they are to be interleaved; the first array will be the first sample in the interleaved data\[char46] Any individual array may be NULL; in this case, silence will be interleaved for that channel\[char46]
.PP
.BR num_channels
specifies how many arrays are in
.BR channel_buffers \[char46]
This can be used as a safety to prevent overflow, in case the stream format has changed elsewhere\[char46] If more channels are specified than the current input spec, they are ignored\[char46] If less channels are specified, the missing arrays are treated as if they are NULL (silence is written to those channels)\[char46] If the count is -1, SDL will assume the array count matches the current input spec\[char46]
.PP
Note that
.BR num_samples
is the number of _samples per array_\[char46] This can also be thought of as the number of _sample frames_ to be queued\[char46] A value of 1 with stereo arrays will queue two samples to the stream\[char46] This is different than
.BR SDL_PutAudioStreamData ,
which wants the size of a single array in bytes\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I stream
the stream the audio data is being added to\[char46]
.TP
.I channel_buffers
a pointer to an array of arrays, one array per channel\[char46]
.TP
.I num_channels
the number of arrays in
.BR channel_buffers
or -1\[char46]
.TP
.I num_samples
the number of _samples_ per array to write to the stream\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread, but if the stream has a callback set, the caller might need to manage extra locking\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

